# Force users onto the latest store version

OTA cannot change `runtimeVersion` (`appVersion`). To move everyone off old binaries, use the in-app store gate.

Source of truth: `packages/ui/src/app-update-policy.ts` → `APP_UPDATE_POLICY.*.minimumStoreVersion`  
Gate UI: `packages/ui/src/app-update-gate.tsx`

## When this is mandatory

- Every **MAJOR** store release (`2.0.0`, `3.0.0`, …) — do not skip
- Also run when the user says everyone must be on the new store version (often after a **MINOR** that is already live)

PATCH/JS-only OTAs do **not** raise the store minimum unless explicitly requested.

## Checklist (after the new store binary is live)

1. Confirm **Play** and/or **App Store** listing shows the new version (e.g. `2.0.0`) for that app.
2. Set `minimumStoreVersion` to that version for **customer** and/or **partner** (only apps in the release).
3. Publish production OTA for **every older runtime still in the wild** (e.g. `1.0.0`, `1.0.1`, `1.1.0`):
   - Temporarily set `version` in that app’s `app.config.ts` to the old runtime
   - `eas update --channel production --environment production --message "Require store version X.Y.Z."`
   - Restore `version` to the current store version
   - Repeat per app (Customer / Partner) and per old runtime
4. Also publish the same policy OTA for the **new** runtime so binaries already on it stay aligned.
5. Do **not** leave `app.config.ts` `version` stuck on an old runtime after publishing.

## Forbidden

- Raising `minimumStoreVersion` **before** that version is live in the store (users hit Update with nowhere useful to go)
- Raising the minimum and only OTAing the new runtime (old binaries never receive the gate)
- Expecting a `2.0.0` OTA alone to upgrade a `1.x` install — impossible; they must install the store binary
- Setting Customer and Partner minima differently “for neatness” unless only one app shipped

## User-facing behaviour

Users below the minimum open the app → pick up the OTA → blocking screen → Play / App Store. They cannot use the app until they update. They must open the app once for the gate OTA to download.
